QuestGuidance.Register("en",76,{
[2401]="70053DBB\n1\tDefeat dire-horns in Rath Dúath (total: 6)\030Defeat Skrithras\tDire-horns can be found in Rath Dúath. You should find and defeat Skrithras, along with other dire-horn goats.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated dire-horns.\n",
[2402]="7001C072\n1\tBring the mushrooms to Glaednoth\030Collect soggy mushrooms (total: 10)\tSoggy mushrooms can be found in the ruins west of Ost Haer. Glaednoth can be found within the ruins of Ost Haer in the southern stretch of Harloeg. Glaednoth asked you to search for soggy mushrooms so he might try to make an interesting meal from them. NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.\n",
[2403]="70071B40\n1\tDefeat Strákhal the Strangler\tA bounty notice asks you to defeat a vicious Orc named Strákhal in Fushaum Sûlm in southern Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.\n2\tReturn to Sálunath with proof of Strákhal's demise\tYou defeated Strákhal the Strangler and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.\n",
[2404]="7006BF7A\n1\tDefeat Suginzi and collect one of his great tusks\tMizâdi Shâra, Queen of Renewed Hamât, has posted a bounty seeking skilled hunters to find and defeat the great plague boar, Suginzi. You are to defeat him and return to her Hand, Numûru, with one of his great tusks. He was last seen south-west of Urmâkh, near Shakhdag.\n2\tBring Suginzi's great tusk to Numûru in Urmâkh\tBring Suginzi's great tusk to Numûru in Urmâkh to collect your reward.\n",
[2405]="700358D0\n1\tDefeat Sulmus and collect his saddle\tSulmus can be found in the Fallows by taking the road directly south, and then searching for eaten prey south of the first split in the road. You should summon and defeat Sulmus, and collect his saddle.\n2\tBring the saddle to Britric\tBritric is in Forlaw. You have collected the saddle of Sulmus, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.\n",
[2406]="70071B42\n1\tDefeat Sóthadar the Trickster\tA bounty notice asks you to defeat a cunning bog-lurker known as Sóthadar who roams Lhámuth in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.\n2\tReturn to Sálunath with proof of Sóthadar's demise\tYou defeated Sóthadar the Trickster and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.\n",
[2407]="7006BF71\n1\tDefeat Tamâhu and collect her mighty stinger\tMizâdi Shâra, Queen of Renewed Hamât, has posted a bounty seeking skilled hunters to defeat the dread scorpion Tamâhu and return with her mighty stinger. She has last been seen west of Urmâkh, near Dûlagig.\n2\tBring Tamâhu's stinger to Numûru in Urmâkh\tBring Tamâhu's stinger to Numûru in Urmâkh to collect your reward.\n",
[2408]="7005976A\n1\tSummon and confront Tansy Haresfoot\tTansy Haresfoot can be found at Sutwarden in the Wildwood. You should summon and confront Tansy Haresfoot.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated Tansy Haresfoot.\n",
[2409]="7003FF77\n1\tTalk to Calennen\tCalennen can be found in central Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale. You have found a bounty posted for Tarlang's Fang and should now seek Calennen for more information.\n2\tDefeat Tarlang's Fang\tTarlang's Fang can be found somewhere in the hills to the south of the Hill of Erech. Calennen has given you all the information he has about the whereabouts of the fierce mountain-lion. You should now track and slay Tarlang's Fang.\n3\tTalk to Calennen\tCalennen can be found in central Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale. You have slain the fierce mountain-lion known as Tarlang's Fang and should now report your success to Calennen.\n",
[2410]="70071B41\n1\tDefeat Thagára\tA bounty notice asks you to defeat a deadly crocodile named Thagára, who roams the Lair of the Shadlúgai in Adagím, and collect a trophy as proof.\n2\tReturn to Sálunath with proof of Thagára's demise\tYou defeated Thagára and obtained a trophy as proof. Return to Sálunath in Sul Madásh to collect the bounty.\n",
[2411]="70009A0D\n1\tTalk to Rowena Parker in Ost Forod\tRowena Parker is in Ost Forod, the old watch-post in the hills of Tyrn Fornech. A poster advertising a bounty for the capture or defeat of a vicious Warg called Thauk caught your eye. If you would like to apply for this bounty, you should speak with Rowena Parker.\n2\tDefeat Thauk at Tûm Fuin\tThe Warg Thauk is in the goblin-camp at Tûm Fuin, north of Ost Forod. You have accepted the commission of the bounty on Thauk.\n3\tTalk to Rowena Parker in Ost Forod\tRowena Parker is in Ost Forod, the old watch-post in the hills of Tyrn Fornech. You have defeated the Warg Thauk and should now report back to Rowena Parker.\n4\tTalk to Basil Gummidge at Ost Forod\tBasil Gummidge is in Ost Forod, the old watch-post in the hills of Tyrn Fornech. You have defeated Thauk and should now report to Basil Gummidge to collect your reward.\n",
[2412]="70044C15\n1\tDefeat the Black Blade of Lebennin\tThe most powerful of Sauron's forces have seized Osgiliath and must be weakened before they can reach Minas Tirith.\n",
[2413]="7001B251\n1\tDeliver the tusks to Sage Hayseed\030Collect perfect boar-tusks (total: 10)\tBoars can be found in the northernmost Bree-fields. Sage Hayseed has asked you to hunt boars for their tusks and return the tusks to her at the camp near the lakes in the north Bree-fields. NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.\n",
[2414]="70044F24\n1\tDefeat the Forsaken Reaver\tThe most powerful of Sauron's forces must be defeated if Gondor is to win the battle.\n",
[2415]="70044C17\n1\tDefeat Lúmithil\tThe most powerful of Sauron's forces have seized Osgiliath and must be weakened before they can reach Minas Tirith.\n",
[2416]="70044F8C\n1\tDefeat the Gloom of Nurn\tThe Gloom of Nurn seeks to claim the crown of the King for Gothmog, who has returned to reclaim the throne of Gondor after his long absence.\n",
[2417]="70044C16\n1\tDefeat Muzgásh\tThe most powerful of Sauron's forces have seized Osgiliath and must be weakened before they can reach Minas Tirith.\n",
[2418]="7003FF76\n1\tTalk to Dírion\tDírion can be found in Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale. You have found a posted bounty for a white stag in Blackroot Vale, and should now speak to Dírion for more information.\n2\tSearch for the white stag in Blackroot Vale\tThe white stag was last seen somewhere in eastern Blackroot Vale. Dírion offered you some advice on where to track the white stag, and you should now seek it out.\n3\tPursue and capture the white stag\tYou should follow the white stag as it flees in eastern Blackroot Vale. The white stag has fled from your approach, but if you give chase, it is possible you might still catch it.\n4\tTalk to Dírion\tDírion can be found in Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale. You were unable to capture the stag due to its agility, but should report back to Dírion in Alagrant.\n",
[2419]="70059774\n1\tSummon and confront Thunash\tThunash can be found at Cotfast in the Wildwood. You should summon and confront Thunash.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated Thunash.\n",
[2420]="70053DB8\n1\tDefeat trolls in Parth Daenath (total: 6)\030Defeat Fuluk in Parth Daenath\tTrolls can be found in Parth Daenath, as can the fearsome beast Fuluk. You should defeat trolls.\n2\tCompleted\tYou defeated trolls, as well as the fearsome Fuluk.\n",
[2421]="7006C6CF\n1\tDefeat Tukûrga\tA bounty notice in Ub Nishir has asked for someone to defeat the kergrim Tukûrga in Tûkurdul to the north-west, near Ashâgir.\n2\tReturn to Neshurga and inform him of Tukûrga's defeat\tReturn to Neshurga in Ub Nishir north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have completed the bounty and defeated Tukûrga.\n",
[2422]="7001B22A\n1\tBring the shells to Walt Whitrose\030Collect thick turtle-shells (total: 10)\tTurtles can be found surrounding the lakes and other bodies of water in the northern Bree-fields. Walt Whitrose would like you to collect turtle-shells and return back to him behind the stones near the falls where the gorge meets the lakes. NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.\n",
[2423]="70071AD1\n1\tDefeat Têzdab the Butcher\tTêzdab the Butcher is reported as having been last seen in the vicinity of Khanâg Gur in An Shêru.\n2\tTalk to Halshûm in Khanâg Gur\tYou have defeated Têzdab the Butcher. You should return to Khanâg Gur to collect your reward.\n",
[2424]="7006C6D1\n1\tDefeat Uzukar\tA bounty notice in Ub Nishir has asked for someone to defeat a ferocious jackal known as Uzukar who has been spotted near Urgudag to the west.\n2\tReturn to Neshurga and inform him of Uzukar's defeat\tReturn to Neshurga in Ub Nishir north of Maurûsh and inform him that you have completed the bounty and defeated Uzukar.\n",
[2425]="700358E2\n1\tDefeat Vîz and collect his helm\tVîz can be found camping near a fang-shaped rock in the Fallows, which can be found by following the road south a ways. You should summon and defeat Vîz, and collect his helm.\n2\tBring the helm to Britric\tBritric is in Forlaw. You have collected the helm of Vîz, and should now return to Forlaw to collect your bounty.\n",
[2426]="7005FFA3\n1\tCollect war dispatches from the Angmarim in Câr Bronach (total: 4)\tAngmarim can be found in Câr Bronach. A bounty posted by Mézto promises a bounty for the collection of war dispatches from the Angmarim in Câr Bronach.\n2\tDeliver the war dispatches to Mézto at Grúmachath\tMézto can be found at Grúmachath. You have collected a sufficient number of wicked daggers and should now deliver them to Mézto for a bounty.\n",
[2427]="70053DBC\n1\tDefeat wargs in Arandor (total: 7)\030Defeat pack-masters in Arandor (total: 3)\tWargs can be found patrolling the waste-lands in Arandor. You should defeat wargs and pack-masters.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated wargs.\n",
[2428]="70053DBA\n1\tDefeat pack leaders in Rath Dúath (total: 3)\030Defeat pack wargs in Rath Dúath (total: 6)\tWarg packs can be found in Rath Dúath. You should defeat pack leaders and pack wargs.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated warg packs.\n",
[2429]="700413BE\n1\tDefeat Orcs in Ringló Vale (total: 12)\tOrcs can be found throughout Ringló Vale. Defeat Orcs in Ringló Vale.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated Orcs in Ringló Vale.\n",
[2430]="7005FFA4\n1\tCollect wicked daggers from evil hillmen in Câr Bronach (total: 8)\tEvil hillmen can be found in Câr Bronach. A bounty posted by Lísek promises a bounty for the collection of wicked daggers from evil hillmen in Câr Bronach.\n2\tDeliver the wicked daggers to Lísek at Grúmachath\tLísek can be found at Grúmachath. You have collected a sufficient number of wicked daggers and should now deliver them to Lísek for a bounty.\n",
[2431]="7001AF99\n1\tBring the skulls to Edith Sweetrose\030Collect wight-skulls (total: 10)\tWights can be found throughout the southern Barrow-downs. The guide, Edith Sweetrose, prizes wight-skulls and will pay you for them. She is camped at the Dead Man's Perch, where the northern Barrow-downs meet the southern Barrow-downs. NOTE: Bounty quests are repeatable quests, but have a finite number of completions. This quest can be completed three times.\n",
[2432]="70053DC5\n1\tDefeat wights in Emyn Duir (total: 9)\030Defeat banner-wights in Emyn Duir (total: 3)\tWights can be found in Emyn Duir. You should defeat wights.\n2\tCompleted\tYou defeated wights.\n",
})
